course: dictionary
lesson: 3783
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Football is a good example: it can name a game, a ball, or a special kind of game in another country. The words around it tell you which meaning fits.
explain: «The Year 3s hid behind the climbing frame whenever Jake walked past, and everyone picked him first at football because they were scared not to.» You do not pick a ball first, you pick people for a team. So here football means the game, played by teams.
explain: «No footballs near it.» The s at the end is a clue: footballs means more than one ball. Try your meaning in the sentence: «No balls near it» still makes sense, so this football means the ball.
fact: Football means a game where two teams try to kick a ball into the other team's goal.
fact: In the USA and Australia, this game is called soccer.
fact: In the USA, football means American football, played with an oval ball that is carried and thrown.
fact: In Australia, football can mean Australian rules football (footy) or rugby.
fact: A football is also the ball itself, and footballs is the plural: more than one ball.
exercise: «The Year 3s hid behind the climbing frame... everyone picked him first at football.» What does football mean here? | *A game played by two teams | A round ball lying on the grass | A school trip | A kind of climbing frame
exercise: In the USA and Australia, what is the game of two teams kicking a ball into a goal called? | Cricket | *Soccer | Rugby | Netball
exercise: «No footballs near it.» What does footballs mean here? | A game between two teams | *More than one ball | Football boots | A football pitch
test: «Danylo tells history like a football fan.» What is a fan? | *Someone who loves and supports a team | A person who sells footballs | A player who kicks the ball | A goalkeeper
test: Which phrase from the lessons means the place where the game is played? | Football boots | Football team | Football match | *Football pitch
exam: «Europa Universalis 5... the way a football video game does not show the players getting tired, bored or cold.» Which meaning of football fits here? | A ball you can carry and throw | A pair of football boots | A football club's shop | *A game played by teams
